      "question": {
        ":question/id": "afc33856-7066-5417-936a-9ed07326cc77",
        ":question/problem": "![](images/b6/b69a99c42bcdbd7e6ae3434862019b792da6bea498fd92a36595722d4fb66995.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "17f7ccd4-172e-5cce-8373-565eb01aeddd",
            ":answer-field/key": "selection",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "2479240c-4181-59ad-9d6a-c1f41507db57",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=36"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "b2dc5091-9c66-5640-8375-4f6b53b91278",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=6"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "d4228851-7c98-55fb-ac1c-17a67fbafeb4",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\sqrt{6}"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "0b019bf8-1bea-5ec9-9a2d-7863fa01fb08",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=36"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "417e211a-bf58-59ba-a39b-b75d997c379c",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "(x-4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=6"
              }
            ],
            ":answer-field/correct": [
              ":answer/id",
              "2479240c-4181-59ad-9d6a-c1f41507db57"
            ]
          }
        ],
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-4,-3)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={6}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
